    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Two buses start together; one returns every 12 minutes and the other every 18.\n\"When will they meet again?\" asked Meena."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "HCF",
     "LCM",
     "common"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The highest common factor (HCF) is the largest number that divides both numbers. The HCF of 12 and 18 is 6.\nThe lowest common multiple (LCM) is the smallest number that both divide. The LCM of 12 and 18 is 36.\nSo the buses meet again after 36 minutes."
    }
   },
